# Cloudflare Pages redirects (copied into dist/ as is; www and the apex alike).
#
# A store discount link, https://www.seemyhealth.ai/discount/<code>/ (cmh-golang's shop module builds
# them; the apps open them). The store is headless, so Shopify's own /discount/<code> on the store
# domain would not reach this site's cart. Every /discount/* path is REWRITTEN (200, the address keeps
# the code) to the static page src/pages/discount/index.astro, which forwards to /shop/?discount=<code>;
# the cart client (src/lib/shopify/cart-client.ts) keeps the code and puts it on the cart through the
# BFF. A plain 302 can't do it: Pages does not fill a placeholder inside a query string.
/discount/*  /discount/  200
